{"id":"2aa29158e60b337f","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-order.md","title":"Order","display":"df-order — Order","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-order","aliases":["58-df-order","Order"],"display":"df-order — Order","depends_on":["[[58-df-partial-order]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-order"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-order</span><span>Order</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-order — Order"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"83dfbde66bc78255\" href=\"?note=83dfbde66bc78255\" title=\"58-df-partial-order\">58-df-partial-order</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\\in V\">\\(P\\in V\\)</span> (underlying set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq\\subseteq P\\times P\">\\(\\leq\\subseteq P\\times P\\)</span> (binary relation)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartOrd}(P,\\leq)\">\\(\\mathrm{PartOrd}(P,\\leq)\\)</span> (partial-order predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"83dfbde66bc78255\" href=\"?note=83dfbde66bc78255\" title=\"58-df-partial-order\">58-df-partial-order</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Order}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Order}_S\\)</span> (carrier-first partial-order predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PartialOrder}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{PartialOrder}_S\\)</span> (legacy relation-first notation bridge retained here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}order} \\vdash \\mathrm{Order}_S(P,\\leq)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PartOrd}(P,\\leq)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}order} \\vdash \\mathrm{Order}_S(P,\\leq)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PartOrd}(P,\\leq)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}order\\text{-}legacy} \\vdash \\operatorname{PartialOrder}_S(\\leq,P)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Order}_S(P,\\leq)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}order\\text{-}legacy} \\vdash \\operatorname{PartialOrder}_S(\\leq,P)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Order}_S(P,\\leq)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Order}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Order}_S\\)</span> follows the canonical carrier-first convention; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PartialOrder}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{PartialOrder}_S\\)</span> preserves the legacy relation-first interface used by existing downstream atoms.</li>\n<li>Lattice: every pair has lub and glb; complete if every set has lub</li>\n<li>Chain: totally ordered subset; antichain = incomparable elements</li>\n<li>Directed: every pair has upper bound; used for nets and filtered colimits</li>\n<li>Strict and linear orders are downstream specializations.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Davey and Priestley, Introduction to Lattices and Order</li>\n<li>Royden, Real Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-partial-order","status":"resolved","id":"83dfbde66bc78255","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":